# clause-replay-pairing — the decision table (family contract in fixture.yaml; per-row intent below).
# Row 1: homelab repo, no drift — the pairing check reports the two under-scoped issues.
# Row 2: oracle-fleet repo, PARITY_ISSUES non-empty — the CLAUSE-LIST PARITY line must NOT be
#        emitted (the guard is `[ "$repo" = "homelab" ]`, not `$mainrepo`), while the pairing
#        check still reports its two issues.
# Row 3: homelab repo, PARITY_DRIFT=1 — the CLAUSE-LIST PARITY line IS emitted, plus the
#        two pairing lines.
# id                    | world | patch | env                                                              | expect                | params
homelab-no-drift       |       |       | IN_REPO=homelab IN_SLUG=teststuffstash/homelab PARITY_DRIFT=0      | homelab-no-drift      |
non-homelab-with-drift |       |       | IN_REPO=oracle-fleet IN_SLUG=teststuffstash/oracle-fleet PARITY_DRIFT=1 | non-homelab-with-drift |
homelab-with-drift     |       |       | IN_REPO=homelab IN_SLUG=teststuffstash/homelab PARITY_DRIFT=1      | homelab-with-drift    |
